# pgAdmin password file, generated from infra/.env
infra/pgadmin/pgpass

# ── Agent working directories and diagnostic renders ───────────
# Both agents render PDF pages to verify a reading against its source. The
# renders are evidence for one decision, not artefacts of the corpus: the
# decision itself is recorded in the database (extraction_assertion,
# page_ocr_adjudication), which is what a reader should be able to check.
# Keeping the images would put tens of megabytes of transient proof in git.
.artifacts/
*-proof.png
*-source.png
replacement-*.png
overlay-*.png

# Scratch downloads and page dumps, whatever the extension.
.tmp-*

# session scratch: fingerprint passes, document-id lists, ad-hoc probes.
# The keepers were promoted to tools/ (fingerprint_segmentation.py,
# compare_fingerprints.py, do-not-replay.txt).
.fp_*.tsv
.fp_*.err
.probe_*
.*_docs.txt
.do_not_replay.txt
.cmp*.py
.lk_*.txt
.replay_docs.txt
.absence_docs.txt
.all_active_docs.txt
.both_docs.txt
.ell_docs.txt
.noc.txt
.render_absence.log

